  "_purpose": "D-One labour standards for the wequote skill. Installation + programming are per-component hours (by labour category); design and project management are percentages. Replaces all previously hardcoded (De Klerk) labour.",
  "_confirmed_with_darren": "2026-08-10 \u2014 per-component hours from public benchmarks + D-One history; design 10%; PM 12.5%; SI host programming fixed per tier; home cinema on the flat 10% design (no extra joinery allowance).",
  "_sources": {
    "authoritative": "NSCA Labor Installation Standard 2022 (nsca.org) \u2014 trade standard for hours per device. Paid; recommended upgrade for exact figures.",
    "camera_cabling": "IPVM 'Estimating IP Camera Cabling Costs' \u2014 0.008 h/ft cable pull; ~2 h/camera all-in.",
    "phase_percentages": "Zigaflow \u2014 programming 15-25% of install labour; PM 10-15% of total labour; rack 4-8 h/12U.",
    "d_one_history": "estimator labour_hours_by_category.json \u2014 D-One's own historical hours (primary source, corroborated against the benchmarks)."
  },
  "_reconciliation_note": "Structured cable drops are priced separately as NETWORK_POINT (R1,650 all-in incl. cabling labour). Per-device install hours below are mount + terminate only; device install + network point together ~ the 2 h/camera public benchmark.",
